GitHub Pages runs Jekyll by default, and Jekyll EXCLUDES every file and
directory whose name begins with a dot from the published output. Without this
marker file, /.well-known/apple-app-site-association and
/.well-known/assetlinks.json are silently dropped at build time and return 404
in production — even though they are committed and visible in the repo.

That is exactly the failure that was observed on 2026-08-09:

  https://www.wellvalet.com/.well-known/apple-app-site-association  -> 404
  https://www.wellvalet.com/.well-known/assetlinks.json             -> 404

The presence of this file (any name starting with .nojekyll, contents ignored)
disables the Jekyll build and makes GitHub Pages serve the repository verbatim,
including dot-directories.

DO NOT DELETE. If it is removed, iOS Universal Links and Android App Links stop
working with no error anywhere except a 404 on the association files, and
password-reset emails silently open in a browser instead of the app.
